  ('ACT', $q$ACT Science$q$, $q$Comparing viewpoints$q$, 'mc', $q$Two scientists explain why some tree leaves turn red in autumn.

Scientist 1: The red color comes from pigments that are in the leaf all summer but are hidden by green chlorophyll. When chlorophyll breaks down in the fall, the red pigments are revealed.

Scientist 2: In most of these trees, red pigments (anthocyanins) are not present in summer leaves. As chlorophyll breaks down in the fall, the tree makes red pigments new. These pigments may shield the leaf from strong light while the tree pulls nutrients out of the leaf before it drops.$q$, $q$Both scientists would most likely agree that:$q$, $q$["red pigments are present in leaves all summer", "chlorophyll breaks down in the fall", "red pigments protect leaves from strong light", "leaves never contain red pigment"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Both mention chlorophyll breaking down in fall. The other choices fit only one scientist, or neither.$q$),
